# nagios_inst — real-world examples

Install Nagios Core 4.x on RHEL/CentOS.
Reference: <https://www.tecmint.com/install-nagios-in-linux/>

## Install required dependencies

```sh
yum install -y httpd httpd-tools php gcc glibc glibc-common gd gd-devel make net-snmp
```

## Create the Nagios user and group

```sh
useradd nagios
groupadd nagcmd

usermod -G nagcmd nagios
usermod -G nagcmd apache
```

## Download Nagios Core and plugins

```sh
mkdir /root/nagios
cd /root/nagios
wget https://assets.nagios.com/downloads/nagioscore/releases/nagios-4.3.4.tar.gz
```

## Custom plugin: check a service is running

```sh
#!/bin/bash
# Nagios plugin - check_service.sh
# Checks whether a program is running
SERVICE=$1

if [[ -z "$1" ]]; then
    echo "Missing parameters! Syntax: ./check_service.sh service_name"
    exit 3
fi

if ps ax | grep -v grep | grep "$SERVICE" > /dev/null; then
    echo "OK, $SERVICE service is running"
    exit 0
else
    echo "CRITICAL, $SERVICE service is not running"
    exit 2
fi
```

Nagios exit codes: `0` OK, `1` WARNING, `2` CRITICAL, `3` UNKNOWN.

## Verify configuration before restarting

```sh
/usr/local/nagios/bin/nagios -v /usr/local/nagios/etc/nagios.cfg
```

